      "keyPoints": [
        "Video models bill per second of successful output, not per prompt, so cost scales with runtime.",
        "The cheapest current tier, Veo 3.1 Lite, is $0.05 per second at 720p with native audio.",
        "A 10-second Sora 2 Standard clip costs about $1; OpenAI's Batch tier halves the rate to $0.05 per second with up to 24-hour latency.",
        "The real cost driver is iteration, not the sticker price: usable shots often take 3-5 generations.",
        "Google notes you are only charged when a video is successfully generated.",
        "Traditional animation pricing guides for 2025-2026 start around $3,000 per finished minute and reach $50,000+ for high-end 3D.",
        "Platform risk is real: OpenAI shut the Sora app on 26 April 2026 and the Sora API is discontinued on 24 September 2026, with no announced successor.",
        "Veo 3.1, Kling 3.0 and Seedance 2.0 are the actively developed alternatives in 2026."
